{"title":"Career roadmap · Investigator","role":"Investigator","summary":"An Investigator gathers and evaluates evidence, interviews witnesses, analyses information, documents findings and supports the investigation of criminal, regulatory, corporate or other cases. A BA in Criminology & Police Administration provides a relevant foundation in criminology, criminal justice, policing, law, investigation and offender behaviour.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Criminology & Police Administration"},"about":[{"label":"The career is broad","text":"graduates may enter government/police investigation, private investigation, corporate investigations, fraud, compliance, intelligence support or research-oriented roles. Some government investigative positions require specific competitive examinations, departmental selection or prior service."},{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Strong alignment, but the exact route depends on the investigator type. A BA alone does not automatically confer police powers or authority to conduct statutory criminal investigations. Government investigative powers depend on the applicable recruitment/service rules."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Criminology & Police Administration","Investigation/Police/Forensics Internship","Investigation Assistant/Research Assistant/Police Recruitment Route","Investigator/Investigating Officer/Investigation Associate","Senior Investigator","Investigation Team Lead","Investigation Manager / Specialist"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build criminal-justice knowledge, investigation methods, evidence handling, report writing and analytical skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Enter an investigation, policing, fraud, compliance, intellige